# Frontend design — CNP Department

## Identity and references

- Treat **Login** (`frontend/src/pages/Auth/Login.tsx`, `.login-*` in `app.css`) as the brand source: deep indigo/navy gradients, warm gold accents on indicators, Inter, restrained borders, premium spacing—not generic “AI dashboard” purple gradients on white cards.
- Extend that identity into authenticated UI via existing tokens (`--accent`, `--text`, `--bg`, `--border`, login navy `#183184` / story blues) without redesigning the login page.
- Before major layout work, skim real product patterns (e.g. [Refero](https://refero.design) categories relevant to education/community dashboards) and adapt **principles** (hierarchy, density, rhythm)—never copy another product’s brand or invent fake reference names in copy.

## Visual quality

- Prefer **editorial composition**: clear typographic hierarchy (eyebrow → title → supporting text), generous but intentional whitespace, asymmetric grids where they aid scanning—not symmetric widget farms.
- Surfaces: light cards on `--bg`, subtle borders, soft shadows (`--shadow`, `--shadow-sm`); avoid heavy glassmorphism stacks and neon glow unless tied to existing login/story motifs.
- Use emoji in nav only where the app already does; new dashboard work should favor SVG marks consistent with login’s line icons where icons are needed.
- No new global CSS files; extend `app.css` with prefixed class names (e.g. `.student-dash-*`).

## Motion

- Motion should **explain state** (enter content, slide indicators, loading handoff)—not decorate idle screens.
- Honor `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`: shorten or disable transitions (see login and `.cnp-loading-*` patterns).
- Route-level loading already uses `LoadingScreen`; avoid stacking redundant full-screen loaders.

## Interaction and accessibility

- Keyboard: interactive cards must support Enter/Space (see `StudentClubCard`); visible `:focus-visible` outlines (login uses indigo focus rings—mirror for new controls).
- Color is not the only signal: pair status with text labels.
- Touch targets ≥ 44px on primary actions where feasible; test sidebar mobile overlay (`AppLayout`).
- Custom cursors only if they clarify drag/zoom—default cursor elsewhere.

## Responsive behavior

- Mobile: respect `mobile-topbar`, sidebar drawer, and reduced padding in `main-content` media queries.
- Grids: use existing `.student-cards-grid`, `minmax` patterns; avoid horizontal scroll for core content.

## Anti-patterns

- Generic three-stat KPI rows with fake percentages.
- Identical card chrome for every role dashboard.
- Bootstrap/Material/Tailwind-style visual language layered on top of current CSS.
- Placeholder “lorem” or invented club/project names presented as live data.
